    # NIGHTSHELF DEEP-ARCHIVE: PROVENANCE REGISTER ☽'NR-IV
    
    *Compiled by ☽'noctmuluevus 'born, Keeper-Registrar, Third Cavern Annex, ☽'secret Sanctninicaesis~*
    
    ---
    
    **PREAMBLE**
    
    This register documents three items under deep-archive custody or active covenant-bind within the ☽'secret Sanctninicaesis~ network. All were handled by this registrar in the brazier-light of the eastern annex; all were weighed, measured, and set down. Authentication follows Pactum∴silenti standards where applicable. Provenance chains are recorded to the extent permitted. Where chains terminate, the termination is deliberate. Notable inclusions: ☽'micseleia' Dagger (condition critical), Veil☽ Sasvaeumis~ (covenant-bound), The Swaleed~ Luminary (status contested). Three shaman-pods gone since the last bone-spiral sounded above us. We catalogue faster now.
    
    ---
    
    **ENTRY I — ☽'micseleia' Dagger**
    *Shadow-steel, fire-core. Custody: The Communion, silk-wrapped, ☽'Saetacaeia-Viamana~.*
    
    It is warm. A hand-span of shadow-steel should not hold heat after centuries in silk, but the captured fire at its core still pulses — faint, orange, visible only when you stop looking directly. The ancestor-bone hilt carries warmth that belongs to the hands that carried it last.
    
    The fracture. It runs the blade's full length, hairline at the tang, widening toward the point to approximately the width of a shed pin-feather. The edges glow where fire-core bleeds through. It will not seal. Netemia Glow-bringer put it there at the Still Pools, driving the dagger through a blood-ward — the steel cracked from inside.
    
    Provenance: Veil-render, Seciae~ carried it longest. See their file. The blade passed to Thung Thrakrek by theft — the cost measured in tunnels we no longer hold. ☽'Iarlocias the Silent recovered it, also by theft, before sealing quarters that would not stay sealed. During ☽'slew Ravium~'s defense, Vorolum~ Vigil drove it into the orca raider Gnarkzund Zaith and the fracture split wider. The hilt fused to her blistered flippers. She could not grip it again.
    
    The fissure widens with each use. The blade is dying. Four have attempted restoration. I will not list what it cost them.
    
    ---
    
    **ENTRY II — Veil☽ Sasvaeumis~**
    *Volcanic glass / shadow-steel composite. Covenant-bound, Pactum∴silenti. Echo∴eliquiae.*
    
    Pick it up. Put it down. I held it eleven seconds and my flippers remembered a cut I never received.
    
    The surface ripples like water under light that is not there. Fire-cores within thirty body-lengths extinguish when it is drawn. The grip is cavern-fungus leather, still warm — not forge-warm. The warmth of the hands that carried it last. See previous holder.
    
    Augur ☽'Milucaum~ crafted it. Augur carried it through the darkening that took the Twilight Shelf and emerged alone. During tunnel-clearing beneath Sleek☽ Caemomot, Augur was documented speaking to the blade seventeen times. Transcription recovered no words. Two of three witnesses later could not remember the incidents. Analysts classify it as having crossed from tool to interlocutor.
    
    Wounds it inflicts do not bleed — they *exhale*. The silence radiates from the edge into the wound itself: Hush☽ Twilight channeled through shadow-steel, the suppression baked into each cut. I have felt the technique manifest here in ☽'secret Sanctninicaesis~ — the pressure thickening, the brazier-flames flattening — and the blade grows darker when it comes. Stains on the flat: penguin and orca both. I did not distinguish which.
    
    ---
    
    **ENTRY III — The Swaleed~ Luminary**
    *Ceremonial vessel, shadow-steel and volcanic glass. The Cell. ☽'slew Ravium~.*
    
    It fits in a closed flipper. It weighs more than it should. It weighs more each time I record it, though I have not lied in its presence.
    
    Three wars scarred into the glass: hairline frost-cracks from Schism (frost-wailed), the jagged scar of The Bra∴conflictu, the concentric spiderweb of The Mbra∴silentiu. Three damage patterns. None have propagated to failure. The flame has burned three colors — gold, red, now a blue so dark it resembles absence.
    
    The Cell maintains this as marginal inventory. The keeper's flippers shake when she tends it. The lantern requires no oil. What the flame costs to keep burning is not recorded here.
    
    ---
    
    **CURATOR'S NOTES**
    
    Pattern: every item arrived through the Incursion damaged in ways that do not reverse. The fracture that won't seal. The blade that darkens. The glass that cracks but holds. Above us the bone-spirals sound again — frequencies we catalogue because three shaman-pods paid for the observation and did not return. The orcas have a word for what follows. We do not.
    
    *— ☽'noctmuluevus 'born, by brazier-light, ☽'secret Sanctninicaesis~*
  CANONICAL_CHRONICLE
  annotation "note_1771587105810_0", anchor: "frequencies we catalogue because three shaman-pods paid for the observation and did not return", text: "The bone-spirals are hunt-songs. Orca assault coordination operates at frequencies that make bones ache — shore-breakers, herders, and finishers each singing their role in the kill pattern. That a Nightshelf registrar catalogued these frequencies as incidental data alongside artifact measurements means the deep-archive had acoustic intelligence on orca tactical structure before the Aurora Stack built its alarm networks. Three shaman-pods lost is not atmosphere. It is three coordinated probing assaults on the approaches to a subterranean refuge. The registrar notes this the way a clerk notes weather. Extraordinary.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771587105810_1", anchor: "the pressure thickening, the brazier-flames flattening", text: "These are corruption symptoms. Every breach-point in the Glow-Fissure network produces identical effects — I have catalogued them at four separate sites. ☽'secret Sanctninicaesis~ sits inside that network. The registrar attributes them to the blade. Perhaps. Or perhaps it is easier to blame a catalogued object than to admit the refuge itself is compromised.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771587105810_2", anchor: "crossed from tool to interlocutor", text: "Analyst language for something the deep ice records without euphemism. Two of three witnesses forgetting afterward is consistent with Hush☽ Twilight suppression, but equally consistent with veil-thinning near active corruption sources — and this site qualifies as both. The analysts classified. They did not explain.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
